# Copy to .env for local overrides. .env itself is gitignored.

# Base path for built assets. Defaults to /WoW_VOD_Review/ (GitHub Pages project
# site). Set to / if you move to a custom domain, which serves from the root.
# VITE_BASE=/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Warcraft Logs (optional — off by default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Death lines on the timeline and log browsing need the WCL v2 API. It is off
# unless you set VITE_WCL_MODE, because the two ways to authenticate have
# genuinely different consequences and the choice should be deliberate.
#
# WCL v2 uses OAuth2, and the client-credentials flow needs a client secret.
# A secret CANNOT live in a static frontend — anything shipped to the browser is
# public and GitHub Pages has no server to hide it behind. So:
#
#   token — each user pastes their own bearer token, kept in localStorage.
#           No backend. Works on Pages today. Tokens expire and need re-pasting,
#           it only works for people who can generate one, and localStorage is
#           readable by any script on the origin. Fine for a personal or guild
#           tool; not fine if strangers will use it.
#
#   proxy — a small backend (e.g. a Cloudflare Worker) holds the client secret
#           and forwards whitelisted queries. The only option that works for
#           people who aren't you. Costs one more deployed thing.
#
# Both use the same client code, so switching is just these variables.

# VITE_WCL_MODE=token
# VITE_WCL_MODE=proxy
# VITE_WCL_ENDPOINT=https://your-worker.example.workers.dev/wcl

# Never put a WCL client secret in this file or any VITE_ variable — everything
# prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the built JavaScript and served to the public.
